shorthand: dev{0,1,3} = 013 026 045 124 156 235 346 ; dev{0,1,5} = 015 023 046 126 134 245 356
cyclic triples == dev{0,1,3} U dev{0,1,5}: True ; disjoint: True
on every line {s,s+1,s+3}: s->s+1->s+3->s (octonion rule e_i e_{i+1} = e_{i+3}): True
cyclic triples through each arc: set = [2]  (2-(7,3,2) design)
Hamiltonian paths in the Paley tournament T_7: h = 189
directed 3-cycles as CYCLES = 14; as (line, rotation) pairs 14 x 3 = 42; the paste's 7 x 3 = 21
counts three rotations of each of only 7 of the 14 cycles. Also each Fano plane has 7 lines and 7 points;
the cyclic-triple design has 14 blocks, so 'lines <-> 3-cycle triads' is 2-to-1 at best.
THM-1370 (canon): the Hamiltonian-path spectrum omits 7 and 21; here h(T_7) = 189 is neither.

